Z||000000||Cozmo||06-07-2001||08:44 AM||||No, this isn't some X-files spinoff... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I've been contemplating swapping the body/interior between the '87 Coupe and the '85 2M6 Targa.<BR>Here's my rationale...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2fierobodyswap.jpg"> <BR>The white Coupe (101K miles) has an excellent condition body and interior.  It's a auto duke with a bad wristpin knock and a bad axle. Also needs new brakes and suspension work.  <BR>The silver Targa (78K miles) has a very ratty body and a DISGUSTING interior. It does have a freshly rebuilt and massaged 2.8, new clutch, brakes and suspension.<BR>My idea is to pull the body and interior off the Targa, paint and detail the chassis then install all the stuff off the Coupe on it.  Then take all the old Targa stuff and put it on the Duke and store it in the yard.<BR>   I do have the rest of the aero moldings to add, even a wing if I want.  <BR>Also, I could paint the Targa top and windshield pillars gloss black like the new Camaros.<BR>Pros?  Cons?  any suggestions?<BR>Thanks! <P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fiero_24||06-07-2001||08:58 AM||||Go for it!  Keep the Targa.  It is not worth fixing the 4cyl.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
